-- title:
--   Exact incidence coverage of the host reporting frontier
-- statement:
--   Fix natural block parameters $h,J$ and finite original-index types with decidable equality. Let $I$ be a finite set of raw items, each containing an original index triple, a retained choice in each block, and a signed-lift label. A wanted label $w$ records the original first index, lift label and global output. Write $\omega(r)$ for the label of an item and $v(r)$ for its length-$J$ word of left-subset choices.
--
--   The host frontier uses the actual ordered child enumeration and exact raw prefix counts. For every $k\le J$ and list $u$,
--   $$
--   u\in\operatorname{frontier}(I,w,k)
--   \iff \exists r\in I:\ \omega(r)=w\ \land\ \operatorname{take}_k(v(r))=u.
--   $$
--   This identifies the prefixes retained by the host with exactly those supported by an original raw incidence.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/ReportingHostFrontier.lean#L55-L68

